Package: python3-libtmux-easy
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         tmux,
Description: tmux sessions from Python, with exact pane exit status
 A stateful wrapper around libtmux for building tmux sessions of named
 windows and panes, with exit status, exit events, output capture and stop
 escalation for the commands running in them, and pytest fixtures that
 launch the processes a test needs.
 .
 Commands: lte-run (supervises a command typed into a pane and reports its
 exact exit status), lte-session (runs a command as the home pane of a new
 dashboard session), lte-close (closes a session gracefully) and lte-key
 (borrows a tmux prefix key for one session). The dashboard sidebar,
 lte-dash, is in libtmux-easy-dash.

Package: libtmux-easy-dash
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         python3 (>= 3.9),
         python3-libtmux-easy (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: dashboard sidebar for libtmux-easy sessions (lte-dash)
 A Textual sidebar beside a tmux viewport: every pane of the session with
 its live status, the selected pane shown fully interactive on the right,
 and keys to stop, rerun and browse them.
 .
 Bundles Textual and its dependencies (MIT, BSD-2-Clause, PSF-2.0) in
 /usr/lib/libtmux-easy-dash, used by lte-dash only: Ubuntu's python3-textual
 is too old.
